OUR COMPANY

Zurich encourages diversity in all its forms! We invite women, people of color, people with disabilities, LGBTQIA+ individuals, and professionals of the best age to apply to our vacancies!

Imagine working in a company that truly cares about its employees, customers, stakeholders, and the entire community involved. Imagine working in a company that is committed to doing the right thing and has as its goal to be the best provider of insurance in the world!

Zurich is one of the leading insurance companies in the world and one of the few that operates on a global scale. With approximately 55,000 employees, we are present in more than 200 countries and territories, dedicating ourselves to understanding the needs of customers and offering solutions for individuals and legal entities, from small businesses to multinational corporations.

Here, we assume the commitment to sustainability, where we have the commitment to displastification, we are attentive to the climate changes, such as floods, we innovate in the development policies and we are increasingly united with the changes of the world. We are enthusiastic about the trust in the digital society and in the way we are constantly automated, looking at the technology and strategies that allow us to have more and more security with our information.

We also foster a culture of diversity and inclusion. Our purpose and values statement is intended to protect, inspire trust, and help our employees reach their full potential! We value and defend what is right and promote opportunities for equality among our professionals, regardless of gender, physical disability, LGBTQ+, race, ethnicity, generations, beliefs, etc. and we are the first insurance company with the Stone Wall Certificate. So, if you believe in diversity as an essential value, Zurich is for you!

We are certified by the GPTW in the list of the best companies to work for, for several consecutive years (2018, 2019, 2020, 2022, 2023 and 2024), cultivating our #JeitoZ more and more.

Come be a Zurich and join our team! Leave your profile in our talent bank!

OUR OPPORTUNITY: ATUARIOR I

The actuary will participate in the usual activities of the reserves area with a focus on local reporting.

RESPONSIBILITIES:

- Generation, treatment, and reconciliation of databases using SAS and Python.
- Calculation of local premiums and claims reserves, analysis of variation and reconciliation of recorded balances.
- Study of Adequacy of the Passive.
- Studies with statistical charts and periodic monitoring.
- Ensure periodic review processes of actuarial studies such as the Average Opening of Claims Reserve, premises used in actuarial reserve estimation, consistency tests of reserves.
- Monitor and respond to points raised by the regulatory body and attend to actuarial and accounting audits.
- Acquire knowledge of the end-to-end process and follow/participate in tests of projects that impact actuarial databases.
- Ensure that the studies and processes are adequately in accordance with local regulations.
- Provide technical actuarial support for direct and indirect management.
- Execute projects related to your area of work and develop new studies on demand/need.
- Actively (in the execution or monitoring of actions) to solve information and/or process problems identified in other areas.
- Perform mapping of process improvements for actuarial analysis and ensure the execution of controls.

QUALIFICATIONS:

- Higher education in Actuarial Sciences;
- Intermediate English;
- Intermediate Excel;
- Previous knowledge in reserves will be a differential;
- Knowledge in Python and/or SAS will be a differential;

